box86-16k (0.3.8+git20260807.0579f8b+16k6) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Port Box64 non-4K ELF32 loader handling to Box86.
  * Handle i386 4K mprotect requests on larger host pages.
  * Build on Raspberry Pi 5 using Box86's existing RPI4ARM64 ARMv8-A/armhf profile.
  * Add 16K synthetic ELF and Steam regression tests.
  * Drop the unnecessary custom RPI5ARM64 CMake patch after validating that the
    existing ARMv8-A profile is compatible with Cortex-A76 and avoids patch drift.
  * Fix Debian arm64-to-armhf cross-build handling by marking native build tools
    explicitly and bypassing dpkg's misleading host-architecture dependency check
    after the builder has verified the required native and ARMHF toolchains.
  * Declare box86-16k as a Conflicts/Replaces successor to the legacy
    box86-steam16k package so upgrades can replace its binfmt file cleanly.
  * Install Box86's upstream /etc/box86.box86rc database explicitly so Steam gets
    its intended BOX86_NOGTK, strong-memory, callret, and emulated-library profile.
  * Add the ARMHF16K native-library closure auditor and ship the observed Debian 13
    Pi 5 incompatible-library manifest with the runtime package.
  * Add reproducible Debian source rebuild and local APT repository tooling for
    16K-compatible ARMHF zlib, BSD, Xau, XCB, elfutils, LLVM 19, and libglvnd.

